 "text": "A shopping list sounds like a small thing, but it can save both money and time. Before I go to the shop, I look in the fridge and the cupboards. I write down what is missing and plan meals for the next few days. I group the list by area, such as fruit, dairy and bread. In the shop, I follow the list and avoid the aisles I do not need. This stops me from buying things on impulse. I also waste less food at home, because I only buy what I plan to cook. It takes only a few minutes, and the habit quickly pays for itself every single week."
